# Rows of a list that are not all the same height, which the window model could not hold until
# now: it counted items and multiplied, so one taller row put the cursor, the highlight and the
# scroll thumb in three different places.
#
# Two things came out of fixing that, and both are on the node detail screen. Watch the group
# titles first and the bars second - the scroll rail in the right-hand gutter is the third, and
# it is measured in the same steps as everything else here rather than in rows.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 220

# Foxtrot Mobile: a handheld on a weak link with a battery running down, so every reading on it
# has something to say.
tab nodes
key down 6
key a
hold 1000

# Down past the actions and into the readings. "Identity", "Signal", "Device metrics" are a step
# smaller than the rows they head and sit on the bottom of their line, so the space the smaller
# glyphs free becomes the gap above them - a section break rather than one more dim row.
key down 12
hold 1600
key down 4
hold 1600

# The bars. A reading with the row to itself can carry the marks its thresholds are at, which is
# what eight cells against the trailing edge could not: SNR is amber past -7 dB with the poor
# mark still ahead of it, and the battery is red past a line drawn where the line actually is.
key down 4
hold 2000
key down 6
hold 2000

# The cursor over a two-step row: one highlight, covering the words and the bar under them.
key up 6
hold 2200

# And a settings section of the same shape, to show the group titles are the list's and not the
# node screen's.
key b
tab settings
key down 12
key a
hold 900
key down 3
hold 2200
